.TH FERMI_SSO_JAR 1 "2026-10-30" "requests-fermi-sso 0.4.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
fermi_sso_jar \- pre\-prime and maintain a cookie jar of Fermilab SSO sessions
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fermi_sso_jar
.RI [ COMMON\ OPTIONS ]
.RB [ status ]
.RI [ SITE ...]
.br
.B fermi_sso_jar prime
.RI [ CREDENTIAL\ OPTIONS ]
.RI [ SITE "...|" \-\-all ]
.br
.B fermi_sso_jar refresh
.RI [ CREDENTIAL\ OPTIONS ]
.RB [ \-\-verify ]
.RI [ SITE ...]
.br
.B fermi_sso_jar verify
.RI [ SITE ...]
.br
.B fermi_sso_jar clear
.RI [ SITE "...] [" \-\-idp "] [" \-\-expired "] [" \-\-all ]
.br
.B fermi_sso_jar sites
.RB [ list | show | add | remove ]
.RI [ ... ]
.br
.B fermi_sso_jar setup
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B fermi_sso_jar
keeps one cookie jar holding live sessions for every site in a catalog of
SSO\-protected Fermilab services, so that scripts can load the jar and
reach the sites without logging in. Log in to each site once, with
whatever credential works for it, and every later process reuses the
result until the sessions expire; then
.B refresh
performs only the logins that are needed.
.PP
The same engine drives two interactive viewers,
.BR fermi_sso_jar_tui (1)
(curses) and
.BR fermi_sso_jar_gui (1)
(Qt), with the same capabilities, and is importable from Python as
.BR fermi_sso_jar.open_session() .
.PP
The catalog of sites is described in
.BR fermi_sso_sites (5).
It ships with the services this package has been run against (Mu2e DocDB,
the Mu2e shift scheduler, Mu2eTalks, SCD Reporting, ServiceNow) and is
extended by writing entries to
.I ~/.fermi_sso/sites.yaml
with
.BR "sites add" .
.SS Site states
Each site is judged offline from the cookies in the jar:
.TP
.B live
the site's cookies are present with an expiry further away than the margin
.TP
.B soon
present but within the margin of expiring (default 30 minutes)
.TP
.B session
present, but only session cookies, whose lifetime the file does not
record. The SSO flow issues mostly these. Use
.B verify
to check them against the network.
.TP
.B expired
present but past their expiry
.TP
.B absent
the jar holds nothing for the site
.PP
The identity provider's own cookies appear as the pseudo\-site
.BR idp .
One identity\-provider session per PingFederate connection (SAML or OIDC)
signs in every site on that connection with no login form, so priming the
first site on a connection is the only login the others need.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BR status " [" SITE "...]"
The default. One line per site with its state, cookie count, time to
expiry and connection. Exit 0.
.RS
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-json
Machine\-readable: the jar path, the per\-site records with a
.B stale
flag, and cookies belonging to no catalog site.
.TP
.B \-\-cookies
Also list the individual cookies, grouped by site.
.TP
.B \-\-stale
Exit 1 if any site is absent, expired or expiring soon, for scripts that
decide whether to refresh.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Only the table.
.TP
.B \-\-utc
UTC timestamps.
.RE
.TP
.BR prime " [" SITE "...|" \-\-all ]
Fetch each site's SSO entry URL through a session loaded from the jar. If
the cookies do not sign in, log in with the credential and save the jar.
Sites are primed in sequence through one jar so the identity\-provider
session from the first login carries the rest. A password is asked for
only when the jar fails and only once per run. Stops when the identity
provider starts throttling sign\-ons. Exit 0 when every site ended signed
in, 1 otherwise.
.TP
.BR refresh " [" \-\-verify "] [" SITE "...]"
Like
.B prime
restricted to the sites whose state is absent, expired or soon. With
.B \-\-verify
the sites holding only session cookies are also checked against the
network, and those that no longer sign in are re\-logged\-in. Prints
nothing with
.B \-q
when nothing was stale, so it suits a frequent timer. Exit 0 when nothing
was stale or every refresh succeeded; 1 when something is stale and no
credential is available, or a login failed.
.TP
.BR verify " [" SITE "...]"
Cookies only, no credential: does the jar still sign in to each site? The
jar is saved when a site's redirect chain added cookies. Exit 0 when every
site signed in.
.TP
.BR clear " [" SITE "...] [" \-\-idp "] [" \-\-expired "] [" \-\-all ]
Remove the named sites' cookies from the jar; with
.B \-\-idp
the identity provider's as well (every site will then log in again), with
.B \-\-expired
every expired cookie, with
.B \-\-all
every catalog site. Cookies belonging to no catalog site are kept.
.TP
.BR sites " [" list "]"
One line per catalog site;
.B \-j
for the full records as JSON.
.TP
.BI "sites show " SITE ...
Every field of the named entries, with the file each came from.
.TP
.BI "sites add " KEY " " URL " [" OPTIONS ]
Add or replace an entry in
.I ~/.fermi_sso/sites.yaml
(or
.BI \-\-file " FILE" ).
.I KEY
is lowercase letters, digits, dots, underscores and dashes;
.I URL
is the site's SSO entry URL (https). Options:
.BI \-\-name " LABEL" ,
.BI \-x " TEXT"
(required on the signed\-in page),
.BI \-D " DOMAIN"
(cookie domain of the site session, repeatable; default the URL's host),
.BR "\-\-connection saml" | oidc ,
.BI \-\-auth " METHOD"
(repeatable),
.B \-\-js\-redirect
(follow a JavaScript
.I location=
stub as ServiceNow serves),
.BI \-\-notes " TEXT" ,
and
.B \-\-test
to run
.B verify
on the new entry.
.TP
.BI "sites remove " KEY
Remove a user entry. For a built\-in site an
.B enabled: false
stub is written instead, which hides it.
.TP
.B setup
Record the account, authentication method, PIN file and jar path in the
env file (default
.IR ~/.fermi_sso.env ,
mode 600), create the jar directory and an empty user catalog, and print
the shell lines that make every tool and script find the same files.
Interactive on a terminal unless
.B \-\-non\-interactive
is given. Options:
.BI \-u " USER" ,
.BI \-a " METHOD" ,
.BI \-\-pin\-source " FILE" ,
.B \-\-store\-password
(prompt and store it in the env file),
.BI \-\-write\-env " FILE" ,
.BR "\-\-shell sh" | csh | tcsh | powershell ,
.B \-\-scheduler
(print a crontab, launchd or Task Scheduler recipe that runs
.B refresh
periodically),
.BI \-\-interval " MINUTES"
and
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run .
.SH COMMON OPTIONS
Accepted by every command, before or after the command word.
.TP
.BI \-c " FILE" "\fR, \fP" \-\-cookie\-file " FILE"
The jar
.RB ( $FERMI_SSO_COOKIE_FILE ;
default
.IR ~/.fermi_sso.cookies ).
.TP
.BI \-\-cookie\-format " FORMAT"
.BR netscape ", " lwp " or " json
.RB ( $FERMI_SSO_COOKIE_FORMAT ;
default: detect).
.TP
.BI \-e " FILE" "\fR, \fP" \-\-env\-file " FILE"
Settings file (default
.I ./.env
then
.IR ~/.fermi_sso.env ).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-env\-file
Ignore env files.
.TP
.BI \-S " FILE" "\fR, \fP" \-\-sites\-file " FILE"
Extra catalog file, merged after the user file and
.BR $FERMI_SSO_SITES_FILE .
Repeatable.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-builtin\-sites
Start from an empty catalog.
.TP
.BI \-\-margin " SECONDS"
Cookies expiring within
.I SECONDS
count as stale
.RB ( $FERMI_SSO_REFRESH_MARGIN ;
default 1800).
.TP
.BI \-\-idp\-host " HOST"
Identity provider host
.RB ( $FERMI_SSO_IDP_HOST ;
default
.BR pingprod.fnal.gov ).
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-debug
Wire\-level logging
.RB ( $FERMI_SSO_DEBUG=1 ).
.SH CREDENTIAL OPTIONS
For
.BR prime " and " refresh .
.TP
.BI \-u " USER" "\fR, \fP" \-\-user " USER"
Account
.RB ( $FERMI_USER ,
then
.BR $USER ).
.TP
.BI \-\-password\-env " NAME"
Read the password from
.BI $ NAME
(default
.BR $FERMI_PASSWORD ).
.BI \-p " PASSWORD"
is accepted but visible in
.BR ps (1).
.TP
.BI \-a " METHOD" "\fR, \fP" \-\-auth " METHOD"
.BR password " (default), " kerberos " or " yubikey
.RB ( $FERMI_SSO_AUTH ).
Kerberos needs a FERMI.WIN.FNAL.GOV ticket; the YubiKey works on the OIDC
connection only.
.TP
.BI \-\-pin\-source " FILE"
YubiKey PIV PIN file
.RB ( $FERMI_SSO_PIN_SOURCE ).
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-no\-prompt
Never prompt for a password.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-save\-cookies
Load the jar but never rewrite it.
.SH PRECEDENCE
Settings resolve as: commandline options, then environment variables,
then the env file, then the
.B settings
block of the catalog files
.RB ( cookie_file ", " margin ", " idp_host ", " user ", " auth ", " pin_source ),
then built\-in defaults.
.SH PYTHON
.EX
import fermi_sso_jar
s = fermi_sso_jar.open_session("mu2e-talks")   # primes the jar if it must
r = s.get("https://mu2e-talks.fnal.gov/api/talks/")
.EE
.PP
.B open_session(site, jar=None, credential=None, ensure=True)
returns a cookies\-only
.B FermiSSOSession
loaded from the jar. With
.I site
the site's entry URL is fetched first; if the jar does not sign in and the
credential (default: resolved from the environment and env file exactly as
the tools do) can log in, the login is performed and the jar saved; else
.B RuntimeError
is raised.
.B JarManager
exposes
.BR status() ", " prime() ", " verify() ", " prime_many() ", " clear() ", " purge_expired() .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.BR FERMI_SSO_COOKIE_FILE ", " FERMI_SSO_COOKIE_FORMAT ", " FERMI_SSO_ENV_FILE ", "
.BR FERMI_SSO_SITES_FILE ", " FERMI_SSO_REFRESH_MARGIN ", " FERMI_SSO_IDP_HOST ", "
.BR FERMI_USER ", " FERMI_PASSWORD ", " FERMI_SSO_AUTH ", " FERMI_SSO_PIN_SOURCE ", " FERMI_SSO_DEBUG .
See
.I env.example
in the source tree.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.fermi_sso.cookies
The jar; mode 600, a bearer credential.
.TP
.I ~/.fermi_sso.env
Settings, written by
.BR setup .
.TP
.I ~/.fermi_sso/sites.yaml
User site catalog, written by
.BR "sites add" .
.TP
.I config/sites.yaml
The built\-in catalog in file form, with the schema documented.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 success (every site signed in, or nothing to do); 1 a site failed to sign
in or is stale without a credential; 2 usage or configuration error.
.SH EXAMPLES
First time: record the account and jar, then log in everywhere once:
.PP
.RS
.EX
fermi_sso_jar setup
fermi_sso_jar prime \-\-all           # prompts for the password once
fermi_sso_jar                        # status table
.EE
.RE
.PP
From a timer, with the password in the mode\-600 env file:
.PP
.RS
.EX
*/30 * * * * fermi\-sso\-jar refresh \-n \-q \-e ~/.fermi_sso.env
.EE
.RE
.PP
Add a site and check it signs in through the existing IdP session:
.PP
.RS
.EX
fermi_sso_jar sites add my\-app "https://my\-app.fnal.gov/login/oidc?next=/" \-x Dashboard \-\-connection oidc \-\-test
.EE
.RE
.PP
A script that wants a ready session:
.PP
.RS
.EX
import fermi_sso_jar
s = fermi_sso_jar.open_session("docdb")
print(s.get("https://mu2e-docdb.fnal.gov/cgi-bin/DocDB/ListBy?days=7").status_code)
.EE
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fermi_sso_jar_tui (1),
.BR fermi_sso_jar_gui (1),
.BR fermi_sso_sites (5),
.BR fermi_sso_probe (1),
.BR fermi_sso_cookies (1),
.BR FermiSSOSession (3)
